improved the understanding of corruption and supported
U4 Partners &#x2013;and the wider development community&#x2013; in
countering it.</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Improved understanding of corruption."></target>
     <actual value="Australian parliament report: Covid-19 and health-related blog posts continue to resonate and inform government policy on Covid-19 vaccines: The blog post on vaccine certificate fraud was used by the Australian parliament for a report on vaccine-related fraud and security risks. USAID guidance note: USAIDs guidance note on how to tackle corruption in the health sector draws on U4s Covid and corruption blog post updates. The Zambian Energy minister, Peter Chibwe Kapala, picked up U4s Senior Adviser Aled Williams thread about our paper on Zambias anti-corruption regime in the renewable energy sector. The minister then posted the papers main points on his public Facebook profile  committing to its message."></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
